drivesync (0.1.0+git20261126.082e743-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The edition's build of DriveSync (Rafael Tosta, github.com/rafatosta/drivesync, GPL-3.0-only), the Google Drive client
    of the final user image (queue row 299). DriveSync has no release yet: built from commit
    082e743ac3eb6755cb4970f768491335281adffa of its main branch (2026-11-26), pinned in the recipe by the archive's
    SHA-256, the commit and the git tree id 78313f02941ac75dd4b6b993923eb09fcbcb5e22, with its Rust crates vendored and
    no network in the build. Debian has no DriveSync, and its own Rust crates are other versions (gtk4 0.11, libadwaita
    0.9, reqwest 0.13, rusqlite 0.40, zbus 5 against the lock's 0.10, 0.8, 0.12, 0.37 and 4).
  * Eight patches of the edition, written in the author's own commit style on the fork branch order299 so he can take
    them, nothing sent: the data directory set at build time (oauth.json and the catalogues under /usr/share), server
    certificates verified against the system's store, a StatusNotifierItem in Plasma's system tray, notifications for
    completed, failed and conflicting synchronization, synchronization held on a metered connection (with a setting,
    off by default), the synchronized folder added to KDE's Places when the person asks, the new strings and the
    desktop entry in the edition's ten languages, and the AppStream licence corrected from a placeholder to
    GPL-3.0-only.
  * Credentials stay in the desktop's Secret Service, as upstream keeps them (KDE Wallet or GNOME Keyring: a Depends);
    there is no file fallback.
  * No Google OAuth client is shipped: sign-in says "Google sign-in is not configured for this installation." until
    /usr/share/drivesync/oauth.json exists (README.Debian).

